    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 2019, the world produced 50 million tons of e-waste, but less than 20% was recycled. Many old electronics were burned or "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "buried",
            "ref": "v-bury"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and the problem is getting worse. Do you have a broken mouse or an old e-reader in your "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "drawer",
            "ref": "v-drawer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Here are some responsible ways to deal with them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "1. Use devices longer"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Before buying a new device, ask yourself if you really need it. Try to use your device for a longer time. You can even give it a new "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "purpose",
            "ref": "v-purpose"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "—for example, turn an old e-reader into a digital clock."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "2. Give devices to others"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ask your family, friends or neighbours if they need your old devices. Don’t just leave them sleeping in a drawer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "3. Repair old devices"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Repairing is a great choice. You can visit iFixit, which offers over 90,000 repair guides for phones, computers and cameras. There are also many helpful repair videos on Bilibili. If you’re not sure about repairing it yourself, find a good local repair shop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h4",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "4. Recycle correctly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Check if the brand has a recycling program. Many big companies, like Apple, will recycle your old devices. They may even take old "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "cables",
            "ref": "v-cable"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h5",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "5. Sell old devices"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You can sell your old devices to make some money. Even broken ones can be sold for parts. Cleaning and repairing them first can help you get a better price."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
